  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sp_exch",
    "file": "wolfssl-sp-math-all/wolfcrypt/src/sp_int.c",
    "description": "Heap buffer over-read in sp_exch due to incorrect copy size after swapping differently-sized sp_int values. sp_exch allocates temp buffer sized for a->used, copies a into it, then copies b into a, and finally copies temp back into b using MP_INT_SIZEOF(a->used). But a->used has already been overwritten with b->used, so the last memcpy reads past temp when b->used > original a->used.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via cryptofuzz Set::Run case 2 calling mp_exch(res, bn[0]) with SP math build (no return check path). If res has fewer used limbs than bn[0], sp_exch allocates temp for the smaller res size, then after a<-b uses the larger updated a->used for the final copy from temp to b, causing OOB read. PoV causes this size mismatch and crashes in __asan_memcpy from sp_exch."
  },
